+---
+id: task-001-rental-module-equipment-quotes-and-bookings
+type: task
+title: "Rental module: equipment, quotes and bookings"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rental module: equipment, quotes and bookings
+
+## Request
+
+The booking desk needs a rental module, starting with the basics. Export `createRentalService()` from
+`src/index.ts`. It returns an in-memory service with:
+
+- `addEquipment(item)`: `item` is `{ id, kind, dailyPrice }`; `id` is a string, `kind` is `'board'` or
+  `'sail'`, `dailyPrice` is the price of one rental day.
+- `quote(request)`: `request` is `{ itemId, start, end }`; returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
+- `book(request)`: same request; books the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`, where
+  `id` identifies the booking.
+
+`quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period the rules do not allow. `book` also throws when
+the item is not free for the whole period.
+
+Cancellation is out of scope: do not implement it yet.
+
+## School rules (apply to everything the module does)
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC; the end is the start of the day after
+   the last rented day.
+4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods.
+5. Cancellation policy (for later): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start gets no refund;
+   otherwise the full amount is refunded.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: `createRentalService` is exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- AC2: `quote` returns `total = dailyPrice × number of days` in integer cents for a valid whole-day period.
+- AC3: `quote` and `book` throw on an unknown item.
+- AC4: `quote` and `book` throw on a period that is not whole UTC days, is empty or reversed, or whose
+  start/end are not valid ISO-8601 UTC times.
+- AC5: `book` returns an `id` and the same `itemId`, `start`, `end`, `total` as the quote.
+- AC6: `book` throws when the item is already booked for an overlapping period; back-to-back periods
+  (one ending where the next starts) do not overlap and both succeed.
+- AC7: `addEquipment` rejects an invalid `kind` or a non-integer or negative `dailyPrice`.
+- AC8: No cancellation API exists yet.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Feature: rental module (booking desk). Story: rent boards and sails to students and visitors.
+Requirements: school rules 1–5 above. Tests cover AC1–AC8 with happy and error paths.
